{%- comment -%}
  Longeva destination detail.

  Renders /pages/destinations/{handle} from the `destination` metaobject.
  Per destination-metaobject-spec.md §4. Reuses existing brand
  primitives (longeva-container, longeva-section, longeva-display,
  longeva-eyebrow, longeva-btn) so the page slots into the existing
  visual system with no new design language.

  Layout (top to bottom):
    1. Breadcrumb              Home > Travel vaccinations > {country}
    2. Hero                    H1 + summary, optional featured image
    3. Recommended vaccines    product cards from list.product_reference
    4. Process                 what happens at your appointment
    5. Traveller advice        rich text (conditional)
    6. Booking CTA band        primary action, final prominent CTA
    7. Further guidance        FCDO + NaTHNaC outbound links (quiet reference)
    8. Clinical review footer  Last reviewed date + reviewer attribution
    9. Cross-link footer       Other destinations in the same region

  The `metaobject` Liquid drop is auto-injected by Shopify when this
  section runs under templates/metaobject.destination.json.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% render 'longeva-brand-fonts' %}
{{ 'longeva-destinations.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{% render 'longeva-destination-jsonld', metaobject: metaobject %}

{%- liquid
  if metaobject == blank or metaobject.country == blank
    assign rendered_in_wrong_context = true
  endif

  assign country_name = metaobject.country | strip
  assign region_name = metaobject.region | strip
  assign reviewer = metaobject.reviewed_by_pharmacist | strip
  if reviewer == blank
    assign reviewer = 'the Longeva pharmacy team'
  endif
  assign reviewed_human = metaobject.last_reviewed_date | date: '%-d %B %Y'

  assign featured_image = metaobject.featured_image.value
  assign vaccines = metaobject.recommended_vaccines.value
  assign traveller_notes = metaobject.notes
  assign fcdo_url = metaobject.fcdo_travel_advice_url
  assign nathnac_url = metaobject.nathnac_url
  assign yf_category = metaobject.yellow_fever_category | strip | downcase

  assign book_label = 'Book a consultation'
  comment
    Every Book button on this page (hero, process step, sticky) routes to
    the on-page booking band below, which renders the Sesami slot picker
    inline with the destination pre-filled and prompts for travel dates
    and length of stay. Anthony (3 June 2026): the previous target,
    /pages/travel-health-consultation-manchester, dropped patients into a
    full services menu, contradicting the page's 3-step promise. The fix
    keeps them on the page and delivers the slot picker directly.
  endcomment
  assign book_url = '#longeva-destination-book'

  comment
    Sibling destinations: iterate all published destinations, filter
    to the same region, exclude self, alphabetise. Quietly does nothing
    if Varsha has not yet populated other destinations.
  endcomment
  assign all_destinations = shop.metaobjects.destination.values

  comment
    Related destination (chunk 4 / ADR ruling B + D): an optional,
    data-driven reciprocal cross-link (e.g. Saudi Arabia <-> Hajj and
    Umrah). Distinct from the region sibling chips. Renders only when
    set on the entry.
  endcomment
  assign related_dest = metaobject.related_destination.value

  comment
    Destination FAQ (Varsha SEO review). Reuses the shared faq_item
    metaobject (question + answer). Count only valid entries (both
    fields non-blank) so an empty or half-filled list renders nothing
    rather than an empty container, and the FAQPage JSON-LD in the
    snippet stays gated on the same condition.
  endcomment
  assign destination_faqs = metaobject.faq.value
  assign valid_faq_count = 0
  if destination_faqs
    for faq_item in destination_faqs
      if faq_item.question != blank and faq_item.answer != blank
        assign valid_faq_count = valid_faq_count | plus: 1
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    Similar destinations (Brief S13, Varsha internal linking). Curated
    cross-region list of other destination metaobjects. Count valid
    entries (a country to label and a handle to link) so the Compare
    block renders nothing until Varsha populates it.
  endcomment
  assign similar_destinations = metaobject.similar_destinations.value
  assign valid_similar_count = 0
  if similar_destinations
    for sim in similar_destinations
      if sim.country != blank and sim.system.handle != blank
        assign valid_similar_count = valid_similar_count | plus: 1
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}

{%- if rendered_in_wrong_context -%}{%- else -%}
<article class="longeva-destination longeva-page longeva-page--light" aria-labelledby="longeva-destination-heading">

  <nav class="longeva-destination__breadcrumb longeva-container" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="{{ shop.url }}">Home</a></li>
      <li><a href="/pages/travel-vaccinations">Travel vaccinations</a></li>
      <li aria-current="page">{{ country_name | escape }}</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <header class="longeva-destination__hero longeva-container longeva-section">
    <div class="longeva-destination__hero-text">
      <p class="longeva-eyebrow longeva-destination__eyebrow">Travel vaccines</p>
      <h1 id="longeva-destination-heading" class="longeva-display longeva-destination__heading">
        Travel Vaccinations for {{ country_name | escape }}
      </h1>
      {% if metaobject.summary != blank %}
        <div class="longeva-destination__summary">{{ metaobject.summary | metafield_tag }}</div>
      {% endif %}
      <div class="longeva-destination__hero-cta">
        <a class="longeva-btn longeva-btn--primary-on-light" href="{{ book_url }}">{{ book_label }}</a>
        <a class="longeva-btn longeva-btn--ghost" href="#longeva-destination-vaccines">See recommended vaccines</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- if featured_image -%}
      <figure class="longeva-destination__hero-image">
        <img
          src="{{ featured_image | image_url: width: 960 }}"
          srcset="{{ featured_image | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ featured_image | image_url: width: 720 }} 720w, {{ featured_image | image_url: width: 960 }} 960w, {{ featured_image | image_url: width: 1280 }} 1280w"
          sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 480px, 100vw"
          alt="{{ featured_image.alt | default: country_name | escape }}"
          loading="lazy"
          width="960"
          height="640"
        />
      </figure>
    {%- endif -%}
  </header>

  {%- comment -%}
    Entry requirements card removed 31 May 2026 per Anthony. Entry
    requirements are immigration border controls, distinct from the
    travel health recommendations these pages exist to deliver. The
    FCDO and NaTHNaC links lower down already route travellers to the
    official entry guidance, so it is not duplicated here. The page now
    leads with recommended vaccines, travel health risks, the
    consultation path and clinical advice. The required_vs_recommended_note
    metaobject field is retained as data (not deleted) but no longer
    rendered, so nothing is lost if the decision is revisited.
  {%- endcomment -%}

  <section
    id="longeva-destination-vaccines"
    class="longeva-destination__vaccines longeva-container longeva-section"
    aria-labelledby="longeva-destination-vaccines-heading"
  >
    <header class="longeva-destination__vaccines-header">
      <h2 id="longeva-destination-vaccines-heading" class="longeva-display longeva-destination__h2">
        Recommended vaccines for {{ country_name | escape }}
      </h2>
      <p class="longeva-destination__vaccines-intro">
        Final cover is confirmed at consultation. Your itinerary, length of stay, medical history and any previous vaccinations affect what we recommend.
      </p>
    </header>
    {%- if vaccines and vaccines.size > 0 -%}
      <ul class="longeva-destination__vaccine-grid">
        {%- for vp in vaccines -%}
          {% render 'longeva-destination-vaccine-card', vaccine_product: vp %}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- else -%}
      <p class="longeva-destination__empty">Vaccine list pending. Please contact us for travel advice.</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </section>

  {%- comment -%}
    Yellow fever cross-link. Renders only where the destination carries
    the yellow_fever_category field ("recommended" = in-country risk,
    "certificate" = entry or transit requirement). Links to the Yellow
    Fever Vaccination Centre hub, which links back here. Wording differs
    by category so it stays clinically accurate per destination.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if yf_category == 'recommended' or yf_category == 'certificate' -%}
    <aside class="longeva-destination__yf-callout longeva-container longeva-section" aria-label="Yellow fever">
      <div class="longeva-destination__yf-inner">
        <h2 class="longeva-display longeva-destination__yf-heading">Yellow fever</h2>
        {%- if yf_category == 'recommended' -%}
          <p class="longeva-destination__yf-text">
            Yellow fever is present in parts of {{ country_name | escape }}, so the vaccine is usually recommended. It can only be given, and the certificate issued, at a registered centre.
          </p>
        {%- else -%}
          <p class="longeva-destination__yf-text">
            {{ country_name | escape }} may ask for proof of yellow fever vaccination if you are arriving from, or have travelled through, a country where yellow fever is present. The certificate can only be issued at a registered centre.
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
        <a class="longeva-destination__yf-link" href="/pages/yellow-fever-vaccination-centre">
          Visit our Yellow Fever Vaccination Centre {% render 'longeva-arrow', size: 15 %}
        </a>
      </div>
    </aside>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Hajj and Umrah cross-link. Saudi Arabia only, since the dedicated
    Hajj and Umrah page covers the Meningococcal ACWY entry requirement
    that applies to pilgrims. Renders only on the Saudi Arabia guide.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if metaobject.system.handle == 'saudi-arabia' -%}
    <aside class="longeva-destination__yf-callout longeva-container longeva-section" aria-label="Hajj and Umrah">
      <div class="longeva-destination__yf-inner">
        <h2 class="longeva-display longeva-destination__yf-heading">Travelling for Hajj or Umrah?</h2>
        <p class="longeva-destination__yf-text">
          Pilgrims must hold a valid Meningococcal ACWY certificate to enter Saudi Arabia. Our dedicated page sets out the required and recommended vaccinations for Hajj and Umrah.
        </p>
        <a class="longeva-destination__yf-link" href="/pages/hajj-and-umrah-vaccinations">
          Hajj and Umrah vaccinations {% render 'longeva-arrow', size: 15 %}
        </a>
      </div>
    </aside>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    What happens at your appointment (chunk 4 / ADR ruling D). Generic
    process scaffold, not a clinical claim, so it sits in the technical
    lane. Strengthens the Destination to Vaccines to Consultation
    journey with a clear next step between the vaccine list and the
    booking CTA. Three native steps, no JS, no CLS.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="longeva-destination__process longeva-container longeva-section" aria-labelledby="longeva-destination-process-heading">
    <h2 id="longeva-destination-process-heading" class="longeva-display longeva-destination__h2">What happens at your appointment</h2>
    <ol class="longeva-destination__process-steps">
      <li class="longeva-destination__process-step">
        <span class="longeva-destination__process-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="longeva-destination__process-step-title">Book your consultation</h3>
          <p>Choose a time that suits you. Tell us your destination, travel dates and length of stay.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="longeva-destination__process-step">
        <span class="longeva-destination__process-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="longeva-destination__process-step-title">Talk it through with a pharmacist</h3>
          <p>We review your itinerary, medical history and any previous vaccinations, then confirm what you need.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="longeva-destination__process-step">
        <span class="longeva-destination__process-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="longeva-destination__process-step-title">Get vaccinated on the right schedule</h3>
          <p>We give the doses with the correct lead time before you travel, and any records or certificates you need.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <a class="longeva-btn longeva-btn--ghost longeva-destination__process-cta" href="{{ book_url }}">{{ book_label }}</a>
  </section>

  {% comment %} {%- if traveller_notes != blank -%}
    <section class="longeva-destination__advice longeva-container longeva-section" aria-labelledby="longeva-destination-advice-heading">
      <h2 id="longeva-destination-advice-heading" class="longeva-display longeva-destination__h2">Traveller advice</h2>
      <div class="longeva-destination__advice-body longeva-prose">{{ traveller_notes | metafield_tag }}</div>
    </section>
  {%- endif -%} {% endcomment %}
   {%- if traveller_notes != blank -%}
  <section class="longeva-destination__advice longeva-container longeva-section" aria-labelledby="longeva-destination-advice-heading">
    <h2 id="longeva-destination-advice-heading" class="longeva-display longeva-destination__h2">Traveller advice</h2>
    <div class="longeva-destination__advice-body longeva-prose" id="longeva-traveller-advice">{{ traveller_notes | metafield_tag }}</div>
  </section>
  <script>
  (function () {
    const body = document.getElementById('longeva-traveller-advice');
    if (!body) return;

    // metafield_tag wraps content in an extra div — get inside it
    const inner = body.querySelector('div') || body;
    const children = Array.from(inner.children);

    const groups = [];
    let current = null;

    for (const child of children) {
      if (child.tagName === 'H3') {
        current = { heading: child.textContent.trim(), items: [] };
        groups.push(current);
      } else if (current) {
        current.items.push(child);
      }
    }

    if (groups.length < 2) return;

    const list = document.createElement('div');
    list.className = 'longeva-destination__faq-list';

    for (const group of groups) {
      const details = document.createElement('details');
      details.className = 'longeva-destination__faq-item';
      const summary = document.createElement('summary');
      summary.className = 'longeva-destination__faq-question';
      summary.textContent = group.heading;
      details.appendChild(summary);
      const answer = document.createElement('div');
      answer.className = 'longeva-destination__faq-answer longeva-prose';
      group.items.forEach(el => answer.appendChild(el.cloneNode(true)));
      details.appendChild(answer);
      list.appendChild(details);
    }

    inner.innerHTML = '';
    inner.appendChild(list);
  })();
</script>
{%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    FAQ accordion (Varsha SEO review). Same native details/summary
    pattern as the vaccine hub and service pages, so it matches house
    style with no JS and no CLS. Renders only when at least one valid
    faq_item (question and answer both set) exists. Each open/close
    marker is the +/minus glyph driven by [open] in the stylesheet.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if valid_faq_count > 0 -%}
    <section class="longeva-destination__faq longeva-container longeva-section" aria-labelledby="longeva-destination-faq-heading">
      <h2 id="longeva-destination-faq-heading" class="longeva-display longeva-destination__h2">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="longeva-destination__faq-list">
        {%- for faq_item in destination_faqs -%}
          {%- if faq_item.question != blank and faq_item.answer != blank -%}
            <details class="longeva-destination__faq-item">
              <summary class="longeva-destination__faq-question">{{ faq_item.question | escape }}</summary>
              <div class="longeva-destination__faq-answer longeva-prose">{{ faq_item.answer | metafield_tag }}</div>
            </details>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </section>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Booking is the primary action, so the CTA band comes BEFORE the
    external guidance links (Anthony 31 May 2026). The FCDO and NaTHNaC
    links were previously above the CTA under an "Authoritative sources"
    heading with a "we recommend reading this before you travel" intro,
    which framed the outbound links as the next step. They now sit below
    the CTA as quiet reference under "Further guidance", with no intro.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section id="longeva-destination-book" class="longeva-destination__cta-band longeva-container longeva-section" aria-labelledby="longeva-destination-cta-heading">
    <div class="longeva-destination__cta-inner">
      <h2 id="longeva-destination-cta-heading" class="longeva-display longeva-destination__cta-heading">
        Ready to plan your travel vaccinations?
      </h2>
      <p class="longeva-destination__cta-sub">
        Tell us your travel date and length of stay, then choose a time. Your destination is pre-filled, and the pharmacist confirms the vaccines you need and schedules the doses with the right lead time.
      </p>
      {%- comment -%}
        Destination booking (Anthony, 3 June 2026): deliver the page's
        three steps directly. The Sesami slot picker renders inline with
        the destination pre-filled as a booking line property, and the
        travel date and length of stay are collected here as booking line
        properties so the clinician sees them. No routing to a services
        menu. Service and variant are the Travel Health Consultation; shop
        id falls back to the theme setting.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% render 'longeva-sesami-button',
         service_id: '15419482145145',
         variant_id: '56910652342649',
         label: book_label,
         prop_name: 'Destination',
         prop_value: country_name,
         ask_travel_date: true,
         ask_length_of_stay: true,
         fallback_url: '/pages/travel-health-consultation-manchester' %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%}
    Compare destinations (Brief S13, Varsha internal linking). Curated
    cross-region links to other destination guides, placed above the
    Further guidance reference links so the internal cross-links sit
    higher than the outbound ones. Renders nothing until Varsha curates
    the similar_destinations list on the entry.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if valid_similar_count > 0 -%}
    <section class="longeva-destination__similar longeva-container longeva-section" aria-labelledby="longeva-destination-similar-heading">
      <h2 id="longeva-destination-similar-heading" class="longeva-display longeva-destination__h2">Travelling somewhere similar?</h2>
      <ul class="longeva-destination__similar-list">
        {%- for sim in similar_destinations -%}
          {%- if sim.country != blank and sim.system.handle != blank -%}
            <li class="longeva-destination__similar-item">
              <a class="longeva-destination__similar-card" href="/pages/destinations/{{ sim.system.handle }}">
                {%- if sim.region != blank -%}
                  <span class="longeva-destination__similar-region">{{ sim.region | escape }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                <span class="longeva-destination__similar-name">
                  {{ sim.country | escape }} {% render 'longeva-arrow', size: 15 %}
                </span>
              </a>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </section>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if fcdo_url != blank or nathnac_url != blank -%}
    <section class="longeva-destination__sources longeva-container longeva-section" aria-labelledby="longeva-destination-sources-heading">
      <h2 id="longeva-destination-sources-heading" class="longeva-display longeva-destination__h2">Further guidance</h2>
      <ul class="longeva-destination__source-list">
        {%- if fcdo_url != blank -%}
          <li>
            <a class="longeva-destination__source-link" href="{{ fcdo_url }}" rel="noopener external" target="_blank">
              FCDO travel advice for {{ country_name | escape }}
              <span class="longeva-destination__source-host">gov.uk</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if nathnac_url != blank -%}
          <li>
            <a class="longeva-destination__source-link" href="{{ nathnac_url }}" rel="noopener external" target="_blank">
              NaTHNaC country guidance for {{ country_name | escape }}
              <span class="longeva-destination__source-host">travelhealthpro.org.uk</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
      </ul>
    </section>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if related_dest and related_dest.country != blank -%}
    <section class="longeva-destination__related longeva-container longeva-section" aria-label="Related travel guide">
      <a class="longeva-destination__related-link" href="/pages/destinations/{{ related_dest.system.handle }}">
        <span class="longeva-destination__related-label">Related travel guide</span>
        <span class="longeva-destination__related-name">{{ related_dest.country | escape }} {% render 'longeva-arrow', size: 16 %}</span>
      </a>
    </section>
  {%- endif -%}

  <footer class="longeva-destination__review longeva-container">
    <p class="longeva-destination__review-text">
      Last reviewed {{ reviewed_human }} by {{ reviewer | escape }}, GPhC-registered pharmacist team.
    </p>
  </footer>

  {%- if all_destinations and all_destinations.size > 1 and region_name != blank -%}
    {%- assign sibling_count = 0 -%}
    {%- capture sibling_html -%}
      <ul class="longeva-destination__sibling-list">
        {%- for d in all_destinations -%}
          {%- if d.region == region_name and d.system.handle != metaobject.system.handle -%}
            {%- assign sibling_count = sibling_count | plus: 1 -%}
            <li>
              <a class="longeva-destination__sibling-chip" href="/pages/destinations/{{ d.system.handle }}">
                {{ d.country | escape }}
              </a>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if sibling_count > 0 -%}
      <section class="longeva-destination__siblings longeva-container longeva-section" aria-labelledby="longeva-destination-siblings-heading">
        <h2 id="longeva-destination-siblings-heading" class="longeva-display longeva-destination__h2">
          Other destinations in {{ region_name | escape }}
        </h2>
        {{ sibling_html }}
      </section>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Sticky mobile booking bar (chunk 4 / ADR ruling D: highest-leverage
    conversion add). Mobile only, position sticky at the bottom, height
    reserved in CSS so it holds CLS at zero. Hidden on desktop where the
    hero + process + CTA band already carry the booking action.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="longeva-destination__sticky-cta">
    <a class="longeva-btn longeva-btn--primary-on-light longeva-destination__sticky-cta-btn" href="{{ book_url }}">Book travel consultation</a>
  </div>

</article>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Longeva destination",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "shopify-section--longeva-destination",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "All visible content comes from the destination metaobject. No section-level overrides; edit the destination entry in Content > Metaobjects > Destination."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Longeva destination",
      "category": "Longeva"
    }
  ],
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["metaobject"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
